-- title:
--   Round-six lemma `depH_le_log`
-- statement:
--   `depH m e ≤ log e / log (m / (m - 1)) + 1`: every level shrinks the width by `(m-1)/m`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6ILSpec`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL.depH_le_log {m : ℕ} (hm : 2 ≤ m) : ∀ e : ℕ, 1 ≤ e →
--       (Bit.depH m e : ℝ) ≤ Real.log e / Real.log ((m : ℝ) / ((m : ℝ) - 1)) + 1
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language: the item-language Prop. 11 interface for a bit network
--
--   * `depH_le_log`, `depH_pow_le`: the recursion depth of `progH` is logarithmic; at the widths
--     `m ^ k` it is `≤ cW k`.
--   * `ilCostR`, **`ILProp11 tab C q T₀ c₁ K₁ K₂`**: at every level `k` (width `m ^ k`), with the
--     KIL5 calling convention `DescIn`, the procedure `tab 0` computes `progH C q (m ^ k)` on the bit
--     stream at cost `⌈K₁ costH C (m^k) V + K₂ (m^k + 1)^c₁ (Bb + 2)²⌉`.
--   * `ilProp11_of_net` (in `R6ILProp`): the item-language Prop. 11 program for a round-six network.
